<title>USA: Northern Telecom says gets Uruguay contract.</title>
<headline>Northern Telecom says gets Uruguay contract.</headline>
<dateline>SUNRISE, Fla. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Telecom Ltd said Thursday that it signed a $15.5 million equipment and expansion agreement with Uruguay's state-owned telephone company, Antel.</p>
<p>In a statement, Nortel said it will expand Uruguay's digitial wireless communications network, adding capacity for 30,000 more subscribers to the network.</p>
<p>Nortel said it will install its TDMA technology beginning in the fourth quarter, and completion is expected before the end of the year.  The company said fixed wireless access will make up two thirds of the entire network.</p>
</text>
